cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite TenderNet v1.1.0 and its version-specific Zenodo record when using this replication package."
title: "TenderNet: data and code for 'Dispersed awards, persistent ties: evidence from Türkiye's public IT procurement'"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aksoy
    given-names: Furkan
    email: furkanaksoy178@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-0228-8202"
    affiliation: Maltepe University
  - family-names: Şimşek
    given-names: Arda
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7969-6351"
    affiliation: Maltepe University
abstract: >-
  Revised data and code for 9,991 EKAP IT contracts (2010-2026).
  Award concentration is measured within title-based product categories, not
  antitrust relevant markets. Repeat-eligible awards show incumbent persistence
  relative to permutation benchmarks. Prior supply is associated with winning in
  a conditional choice model; future-supplier diagnostics caution against attributing
  these associations to a causal effect or identifying mechanism shares. Currency
  corrections use cached TCMB tender-date valuation proxies and explicitly flag
  missing currency labels assumed to be TRY.
keywords:
  - public procurement
  - incumbency
  - vendor lock-in
  - market concentration
  - bipartite networks
  - Türkiye
  - EKAP
